<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================
  cr-dotnet-0010: Web.config Transformation File — DEPRECATED
  ============================================================
  This Web.Release.config transformation file has been superseded
  by runtime environment variables and AWS Systems Manager (SSM)
  Parameter Store as part of the cloud-readiness remediation for
  rule cr-dotnet-0010 (Web.config Transformations).

  REASON FOR DEPRECATION:
  Build-time Web.config XDT transformations bake environment-
  specific configuration into the deployment artifact, violating
  the 12-factor app principle III (Config) and preventing true
  immutable deployments in AWS cloud environments.
  The original "RemoveAttributes(debug)" transform on
  <compilation> is no longer needed because the debug flag is
  controlled at runtime via the ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT /
  ASPNET_ENV environment variable.

  REPLACEMENT STRATEGY — Environment Variables & AWS SSM:
  All configuration values previously managed via XDT transforms
  are now injected at runtime through:

    1. Environment Variables (12-factor app, Principle III)
       Set the following environment variables in your AWS
       deployment environment (ECS task definition, Elastic
       Beanstalk environment, or EC2 instance):

         DB_CONNECTION_STRING
           The full ADO.NET connection string for the database.
           In AWS, point this to the Amazon RDS Proxy endpoint:
           "Server=<rds-proxy-endpoint>,1433;Database=tourdb;
            User Id=<user>;Password=<secret>;
            TrustServerCertificate=True;
            Max Pool Size=100;Min Pool Size=5;"

         S3_BUCKET_NAME
           Name of the Amazon S3 bucket used for file uploads
           (Tour_pics, profile pictures, etc.).

         AWS_REGION
           AWS region for SDK clients (e.g., "us-east-1").

         ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT  (or ASPNET_ENV for .NET Fx)
           Set to "Development" locally, "Production" in AWS.
           When set to "Production", ASP.NET automatically
           disables debug compilation — no XDT transform needed.

    2. AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store
       Store sensitive values (passwords, API keys) as
       SecureString parameters under a path hierarchy, e.g.:
         /tour-management/prod/db-connection-string
         /tour-management/prod/s3-bucket-name
       Retrieve them at application startup via the AWS SDK
       (Amazon.SimpleSystemsManagement NuGet package) and
       populate the IConfiguration / ConfigurationManager
       before the application begins serving requests.

    3. AWS Secrets Manager (for credentials)
       Database credentials and other secrets should be stored
       in AWS Secrets Manager and rotated automatically.
       Reference the secret ARN in the ECS task definition or
       Elastic Beanstalk configuration rather than embedding
       credentials in any configuration file.

  APPLICATION CODE CHANGES (cr-dotnet-0010):
  The following files have been updated to read configuration
  from environment variables first, falling back to
  appsettings.json / Web.config for local development only:

    - AddTour.aspx.cs      (line 21) — GetConnectionString()
    - Order.aspx.cs        (line 21) — GetConnectionString()
    - SignUpForm.aspx.cs   (line 21) — GetConnectionString()
    - TourCrud.aspx.cs     (line 25) — GetConnectionString()
    - userlogin.aspx.cs    (line 25) — GetConnectionString()

  Pattern used in each file:
    private string GetConnectionString()
    {
        return Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("DB_CONNECTION_STRING")
            ?? _configuration.GetConnectionString("dbconnection");
    }

  This file is intentionally left without active XDT transforms.
  It is retained in the project only for source-control history
  and to satisfy the MSBuild DependentUpon relationship with
  Web.config. No XDT transformations will be applied during build.
  ============================================================
-->
<configuration xmlns:xdt="http://schemas.microsoft.com/XML-Document-Transform">
  <!--
    No XDT transformations are defined here.
    All environment-specific configuration is managed via
    environment variables and AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store
    as described in the comments above.

    Previously this file contained:
      <compilation xdt:Transform="RemoveAttributes(debug)" />
    This is no longer needed. Debug mode is controlled at runtime
    by the ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT / ASPNET_ENV environment variable.
    Set ASPNET_ENV=Production in your AWS deployment environment.
  -->
</configuration>
